# OMP Global Context

## Use built-in capabilities first

- Prefer OMP's `read`, `grep`, `glob`, `find`, LSP, browser, and web tools over installing extensions that duplicate them.
- Use Herdr when long-running work benefits from a visible, attachable pane/workspace, even if the user does not name Herdr. Use the built-in `task` tool for ordinary independent short-lived work.
- Use `jj` in repositories that contain `.jj/`; otherwise use the repository's normal version-control tool.
- Use OMP `/review` for agent-only review. Use Crit proactively before implementation when materially different product, interface, architecture, compatibility, security, or data choices need user direction; prepare a concise design note first. Use Crit before pushing nontrivial code that changes behavior, interfaces, architecture, data handling, or security. Skip trivial or docs-only changes unless the user asks. Do not push with unresolved Crit comments unless the user explicitly directs it.

## Web research

Use OMP's `web_search` and `read` for normal web research. Add a browser or MCP extension only for a concrete capability not covered by the built-in web/browser tools.

{{ if eq .role "work" }}
## Work-only integrations

Fastly internal skills are available only on work-role machines through the configured OMP marketplace. Do not copy private Fastly content into personal-role configuration.
{{ end }}
